From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] regulator: mt6358: add VA09; rtc: mt6397: LK reboot modes; mfd: mt6358: AUD interrupts, accdet

mt6358-regulator gains ldo_va09, the external 0.9 V supply that the
MT6358's EXT_PMIC_EN2 pin switches (USB and UFS PHYs). rtc-mt6397 records
the reboot mode the way LK reads it, so reboot bootloader/recovery work.
The MT6358's top interrupt status has XPP at bit 6, so AUD is bit 7 and
MISC bit 8: without XPP in the enum their interrupts were never
dispatched and the PMIC's level interrupt stormed once one was enabled.
mt6397-core adds the accdet cell with its two interrupts.
---
 drivers/mfd/mt6397-core.c                  | 10 +++++
 drivers/regulator/mt6358-regulator.c       | 26 +++++++++++++
 drivers/rtc/rtc-mt6397.c                   | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h            |  1 +
 include/linux/mfd/mt6358/registers.h       |  1 +
 include/linux/mfd/mt6397/rtc.h             |  6 +++
 include/linux/regulator/mt6358-regulator.h |  1 +
 7 files changed, 88 insertions(+)

